{
  "title": { "en": "Defining “or”" },
  "tray": "proof",
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "“Or” can be defined the same way: “A or B” is “for every sentence R, if R follows from A and R follows from B, then R”, written ∀R. (A → R) → ((B → R) → R)."
      }
    }
  ],
  "after": {
    "en": "A declaration gives the intro rules and the elimination rule is made from them; a definition like this writes down the elimination rule, and the intro rules are proved from it. Both roads give the same rules."
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "h-or-make_1",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "Making it" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "A" }, "goal": "∀R. (A → R) → ((B → R) → R)" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "Bus", "B": "Bike", "C": "OnTime" }, { "A": "Sat", "B": "Sun", "C": "Rest" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "A for-any box takes R; inside, the goal has two layers of “if … then …”."
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "s = allI[x=R](body: f) {",
        "  body {",
        "    f = impI[A=\"A -> R\"](body: g) {",
        "      body {",
        "        g = impI[A=\"B -> R\"](body: m) {",
        "          body {",
        "            m = mp(f.body, p)",
        "          }",
        "        }",
        "      }",
        "    }",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "goal <- s"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "h-or-make_2",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "Using it" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "∀R. (A → R) → ((B → R) → R)", "q": "A → C", "r": "B → C" }, "goal": "C" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "Bus", "B": "Bike", "C": "OnTime" }, { "A": "Sat", "B": "Sun", "C": "Rest" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "The conclusion wanted is C: put C in for R, then hand it the two moves in turn."
        }
      ],
      "solution": ["e = allE[t=C](p)", "m1 = mp(e, q)", "m2 = mp(m1, r)", "goal <- m2"]
    }
  ]
}
